        "original_id": "c8d899c4-bf0d-58f0-b0be-6d6485c4dbe7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Bryan Caplan, Patrick Michaels, Ed Crane, Murray Rothbard, Charles Koch\n- Organizations: George Mason University, Mercatus Center, Cato Institute, Freakonomics, Greening Earth Society, Western Fuels Association, Koch Industries\n- Publications: EconLog, World Climate Report\n- Roles: economist, professor of economics, research fellow, adjunct scholar, senior fellow\n- Topics: libertarian think tanks, environmental studies\n\nFacts:\n- Bryan Douglas Caplan was born on April 8, 1971, and is an American economist.\n- The Cato Institute was founded in 1974 as the Charles Koch Foundation by Ed Crane, Murray Rothbard, and Charles Koch.\n- The Cato Institute is an American libertarian think tank headquartered in Washington, D.C.\n- Charles Koch is chairman of the board and chief executive officer of Koch Industries.\n- Bryan Caplan is a professor of economics at George Mason University, a research fellow at the Mercatus Center, an adjunct scholar at the Cato Institute, a frequent contributor to Freakonomics, and the publisher of the blog EconLog.\n- Patrick Michaels is a senior fellow in environmental studies at the Cato Institute.\n- World Climate Report is a newsletter edited by Patrick Michaels.\n- World Climate Report was produced by the Greening Earth Society, a non-profit organization created by the Western Fuels Association.",
